    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, Economics 2022 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "econ-2022-hl-q16-b-ii", topicId: "economics-0-2", conceptId: "low-carbon-strategy-government",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2022 HL Q16(b)(ii) — Irish government",
    stem: "The UN Secretary-General said the Working Group's report for sustainability was a code red for humanity. The alarm bells are deafening, and the evidence is irrefutable.",
    questionText: "Suggest strategies that could be employed by the Irish government and Irish citizens to aid with the transition to a low carbon economy. Irish Government:",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"1 @ 7","answer":1,"ofParts":7,"perPart":7}, totalMarks: 7,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "A strategy for Irish government — any one", marks: 7, contextNote: "One developed strategy for Irish government, 7 marks (4 + 3). The question asks for both actors and the scheme prices each 7.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":1,"perOption":7,"options":["Increased incentives to purchase electric cars. If the government can provide incentives, financial or otherwise, to Irish citizens to make the switch to electric vehicles it may increase the uptake of these vehicles in Ireland.","Increased environmental audits of production methods of Irish firms. If the department of the environment is more stringent in its review of how firms do business in Ireland it may deter firms from producing in environmentally harmful ways.","Increased penalties for firms which have a negative environmental impact. Firms which produce in environmentally harmful ways could be hit with large financial penalties by the government.","Tax breaks for firms which produce in environmentally friendly production methods. This financial incentive may be enough to encourage a firm to amend their production practices.","Increased funding for research and development in green areas. The government could help support university initiatives across Ireland to try and help plan for a green future.","Increased funding for educational programmes for the youth. Increased funding for educational programs for the youth may help to prepare the next generation on how to approach this crisis.","Improve infrastructure for electric vehicles. If the government provides more charging points for electric vehicles it will better allow Irish motorists to transition to less environmentally harmful vehicles."]} },
    ],
