    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, Economics 2023 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "econ-2023-hl-sa-q6-b", topicId: "economics-3-1", conceptId: "canons-of-taxation",
    section: "A", questionRef: "2023 HL Section A Q6(b)",
    questionText: "Outline three canons/principles of taxation which are achieved through the use of direct taxes.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"6","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 6,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "Certainty: it should be clear and unambiguous to the taxpayer the amount they are required to pay and the reason for doing so.\n\nConvenience: the tax such be levied at a time and in a manner which is most convenient for the taxpayer to pay.\n\nEquity: the tax system should operate fairly. An equitable tax system should take a larger amount from those who are more able to pay than others.\n\nEconomy: the cost of tax collection should be far exceeded by the amount of tax which is collected.\n\nNot act as a disincentive to save/work/invest: no tax should negatively affect those willing to supply their labour / or their ability to save or discourage entrepreneurs from investing.\n\nEvasion should be impossible: otherwise the tax is not effective in raising revenue.", marks: 6, contextNote: "Three canons, 6 marks overall, with no published split per canon; these are the scheme’s examples.\n\nIrish source note: the paper says indirect taxes (cánacha indíreacha). The official scheme acknowledges a translation error and accepts discussion of any taxation principles. Give the three principles requested; the task remains worth 6 marks.", openList: true },
    ],
