    id: "econ-2024-hl-q12-a-ii", topicId: "economics-3-0", conceptId: "effects-of-the-hidden-economy",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2024 HL Q12(a)(ii)",
    stem: "Revenue actively challenges all forms of hidden economic activity.",
    questionText: "Outline two effects on the Irish economy of an increase in activities in the hidden economy.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"2 @ 5","answer":2,"ofParts":6,"perPart":5}, totalMarks: 10,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "An effect of a growing hidden economy — any two", marks: 10, contextNote: "Two effects, 5 marks each.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":5,"options":["Loss of tax revenue to the government/pressure on government services: Revenues which are essential to the provision of state services are lost to the exchequer. These could have been used by the government in various ways. The loss of revenue to the state the government may have to cut spending and find additional sources of tax revenue and/or reduce the volume of services which it provides and/or increase borrowing.","Decline in legitimate business activity: Legitimate businesses will suffer a decline in sales, leading to possible job losses and a decline in economic activity.","Increased government expenditure on enforcement: To curb the activities of the shadow economy the government may have to increase spending on enforcement which will lead to pressure on the state’s finances.","Increased crime levels: An increase in shadow/hidden economic activities results in increased crime and may instil fear in citizens.","Standards of products/services: Because of lack of regulation, products may be unsafe or harmful to consumers.","Increase in employment in the hidden economy: More people may opt to seek employment in this economy i.e. cleaning services. Hindering legitimate business."]} },
    ],
