    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, Economics 2024 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "econ-2024-hl-q16-c-iii-advantage", topicId: "economics-3-1", conceptId: "advantages-and-disadvantages-of-indirect-tax",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2024 HL Q16(c)(iii)",
    stem: "To fund more expenditure into the future, the Minister for Finance is considering raising tax revenue through a policy of increasing indirect taxation.",
    questionText: "Discuss the economic advantages and disadvantages of increasing indirect taxation.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"2 @ 6","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 12,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-advantage", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "An advantage", marks: 6, contextNote: "Complete BOTH headings: two points at 6 marks each, and the scheme requires a MINIMUM of ONE advantage and one disadvantage. One advantage, 6 marks.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":1,"perOption":6,"options":["Low collection cost – more convenient collection because the taxes are collected by retailers.","Evasion is more difficult – it is harder to avoid indirect taxes as these taxes are included in the price of the good or service.","Less distortionary / no disincentive to work - VAT does not discourage work unlike increases in income tax.","Possibly more ‘acceptable’ than alternatives - it may be easier for government to raise tax revenue through indirect tax rather as these taxes are included in the price of the good or service. Alternatives such as increasing income tax; chargers for services may be more unpopular.","Used by government to change consumption patterns – a government can change consumption patterns (aligning private and social costs) by increasing indirect taxes e.g. reduce consumption of harmful products e.g. sugar tax and the carbon tax.","Acts as a built-in stabiliser – indirect taxes take more out of the economy when the economy is performing well and leaves more money in the economy when it is not performing as strong. It is a built-in stabiliser."]} },
    { id: "r-disadvantage", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "A disadvantage", marks: 6, contextNote: "One disadvantage, 6 marks.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":1,"perOption":6,"options":["Will increase inflation – Indirect taxes increase the prices of goods and services and hence the cost of living, possibly causing demands for further wages increases.","Regressive / inequitable – lower income groups may end up paying a greater proportion of their income in this form of tax because they spend a greater proportion of their income on necessities.","Revenue not as certain – the revenue collected is not as predictable as that from direct taxation which could hinder government planning / planning.","Burden of collection with retailers – retailers now act as revenue collectors and procedures must be put into practice to collect, record and remit the revenue. This is a further cost for firm and may deter business set-up."]} },
    ],
