    year: 2026, level: "higher",
    paperFileid: "LC034ALP000EV",
    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, Economics 2026 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "econ-2026-hl-sa-q4-c", topicId: "economics-1-1", conceptId: "benefits-of-second-hand-clothing-apps",
    section: "A", questionRef: "2026 HL Section A Q4(c)",
    questionText: "Outline two ways the use of online second-hand clothing apps, like Vinted and Depop, may benefit consumers of second-hand clothing.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"2 @ 3","answer":2,"ofParts":7,"perPart":3}, totalMarks: 6,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "A benefit for consumers — any two", marks: 6, contextNote: "Two benefits, 3 marks each. Answer either (b) or (c).", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":3,"options":["Lower prices and better value – online second-hand apps increase competition between sellers and reduce overhead costs compared to physical shops. This often results in lower prices, which allows consumers to purchase clothing at better value than new items.","Greater choice and variety – the apps give consumers access to many sellers across Ireland and internationally. This significantly increases the range of brands, styles, sizes, and unique items available compared to local second-hand shops, e.g. vintage /retro / niche items.","Increased convenience and accessibility – consumers can browse, compare and purchase second-hand clothing at any time online. This removes the need to travel to physical shops and makes second-hand shopping more accessible.","Improved price transparency and comparison – the apps allow consumers to compare prices for similar items easily. This helps consumers make more informed purchasing decisions and avoid overpaying. Some apps allow buyers to message sellers to negotiate prices or bundle items, which helps consumers benefit from better value.","Access to detailed information and reviews – listings on apps typically include photos, descriptions, and seller ratings. This reduces uncertainty about quality and reliability, which increases consumer confidence when buying second-hand clothing.","Reduced search time and effort – search filters for size, brand, price, and condition allow consumers to find suitable items quickly. This reduces the time and effort involved in finding suitable second-hand clothing.","Environmental benefits passed on to consumers – by extending the life of clothing, online second-hand apps reduce textile waste / the environmental damage of fast fashion. Consumers benefit by making more environmentally sustainable choices without sacrificing affordability or style."]} },
    ],
